            <ArticleTitle>[Use of zoledromic acid on pain control in stages M1b of prostate cancer].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1100-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To probe the use of Zoledromic acid in the control of the pain due to bone methastasis of a prostate cancer.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">We included in our study 37 consecutive patients diagnosed of prostate cancer who developed bone methastasis during 2005 and 2006 to whom we gave a 4 mg dose of Zoledromic acid during a mean time of 10.24 months.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">We observed a complete control of the pain in 8 of the 20 patients, and partially in 6 of those patients. We did not evaluate any adverse reaction due to this treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">We still yet to know whether the administration of this treatment in the early stages of the prostate cancer could prevent or retard the appearance of bone methastasis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
